# @koolee/db — used ONLY by the drizzle-kit CLI and the seed script.
# Apps pass their own env at runtime; this package reads nothing in production.
#
# Copy to `.env` (NOT `.env.local` — drizzle-kit's convention, and what
# drizzle.config.ts loads).
#
# `pnpm db:generate` needs NOTHING; it diffs the schema offline.
# `pnpm db:migrate` and `pnpm db:studio` use DIRECT_DATABASE_URL (port 5432).
# `pnpm seed` uses DATABASE_URL.
#
# Never point DIRECT_DATABASE_URL at the Supavisor pooler — the migrator takes
# an advisory lock and issues DDL, which transaction pooling cannot support.

# DEFAULT TARGET: LOCAL. Keep these pointed at the local Supabase stack so a
# bare `pnpm db:migrate` / `pnpm seed` can never silently land on hosted —
# that accident has happened. Target hosted only via an inline override
# (the shell always beats this file, see src/migrate.ts / drizzle.config.ts):
#
#   DIRECT_DATABASE_URL='postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@...pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres' pnpm db:migrate
#
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres

# Hosted values, for the inline override above — Supabase → Connect → Database:
#   pooled (TRANSACTION mode), port 6543 → DATABASE_URL (app runtime only)
#     postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
#   SESSION pooler, port 5432 → DIRECT_DATABASE_URL (migrations/DDL; stable
#   backend + IPv4-reachable — the db.<ref>.supabase.co "direct" host is
#   IPv6-only and unreachable from e.g. GitHub runners)
#     postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
